<title>UK: Adtranz forced to cut 188 UK jobs.</title>
<headline>Adtranz forced to cut 188 UK jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>European railway engineering group Adtranz (ABB Daimler-Benz Transportation) said on Thursday that it had &quot;no option&quot; but to reduce the scale of its rail maintenance operations in the UK and make 188 redundancies.  </p>
<p>Adtranz said it was &quot;extremely disappointed&quot; to announce the redundancies, which will be made at its railway maintenance workshop in Doncaster, Northern England.</p>
<p>It said that changes in the UK railway market have affected the traditional workload at Doncaster.</p>
<p>The redundanacies will be carried out on a phased basis up to the end of March 1997.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
